Z||000000||LAMBO||05-01-2000||10:42 PM||||Hello Forum Members...just bought my first Fiero today ('85 2M6 SE). Thought it would be the right occasion to join the forum now (I've been reading it for a couple months and I think this is an invaluable info resource). Paid $500 for her...she's a little rough looking but runs great! Silver, auto, most of the options. Destined for an engine swap at some point in the future, but going to use her for commuting right now. Good bye Ford Aspire! Hello passing other cars uphill, instead of the other way around!!! ||||reg||7
Z||000001||stimpy||05-02-2000||07:34 AM||||Welcome!<BR>(welcome wagon stimpy!,&lt;-HEH)<P>$500 is a pretty good deal- how much stuff do you need to get it looking good? Chances are someone has it around here.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LAMBO||05-02-2000||08:58 AM||||Hello Stimpy. Thanks for the welcome. At first glance, she has a white front nose (bumper?) that needs to be replaced, a missing luggage rack tail piece, and some fading on the top surfaces with the usual chips and scratches for an '85 model car. It wasn't running when I picked it up because it lacked an alternater/water pump belt but that was easy. The guy I bought it from parked it because he thought it was going to be a major chore to fix, probably why I got it bought right.||||reg||10
